Thanks for the repro. I couldn't run duplicate searches or check the source here, so this is based on reading your code.

This looks like standard Node behavior, not a Vitest bug. `foo()` rejects *during* `await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(100)`. At that point nothing has handled the promise yet, because `.rejects` is attached on the next line. Node emits `unhandledRejection` and Vitest reports it, even though the assertion passes later.

Attach the handler before advancing the timers:

```ts
const result = foo();
const assertion = expect(result).rejects.toThrow('boom');
await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(100);
await assertion;
```

If you still see the unhandled error with this ordering, please reply with an updated repro. I'd then treat it as a bug.
